content.text:
Implemented [`Agents/stockResearch/toolDeterminerAgent.ts`](Agents/stockResearch/toolDeterminerAgent.ts).

### Input
- **`userPrompt`** — investment / research question  
- **`instrument`** — full BOD row (`instrument_key`, …) or Prisma-style camelCase instrument (normalized via `normalizeStockResearchInstrument`)

### Output (`ToolDeterminerResult`)
- **`upstox`** — booleans for each key in `upstoxApis` (except `assertMarginApiNotUsed` and `testUpstoxConnection`)
- **`serp`** — booleans for each key in `serpEngines` (9 engines)
- **`reasoning`**, **`instrument`**, **`model`**

### Behavior
- LLM structured output (`toolDeterminerModelOutputSchema`) using catalogs built from `@/services/upstox/index` and `@/SERP/index`
- **`applyInvestResearchMinimums`** — when the prompt looks like invest/deep analysis, turns on fundamentals (equity + ISIN), quotes/history/news, Serp finance/news/web, and derivatives tools (F&O) as appropriate
- Streaming Upstox tools stay off unless the user asks for live feed

### Usage

```ts
import { runToolDeterminerAgent } from "@/Agents/stockResearch/toolDeterminerAgent";

const plan = await runToolDeterminerAgent({
  userPrompt: "I want to invest in this stock — give me as much detail as possible.",
  instrument: marutiInstrumentRow, // BOD or DB shape
});

if (plan.upstox.getCompanyProfile) {
  // call upstoxApis.getCompanyProfile.fn(...)
}
if (plan.serp.searchGoogleFinance) {
  // serpEngines.searchGoogleFinance.fn(...)
}
```

Env model: `STOCK_RESEARCH_TOOL_DETERMINER_MODEL` → `DETERMINER_MODEL` → default OpenAI model.

[REDACTED]

